    <string name="section_how_it_works">How it works</string>
    <string name="how_it_works_body">Motion sickness happens when your inner ear feels the car speeding up, braking and turning while your eyes, fixed on a still screen, report no motion. The cues move the way your body is pushed: back when the car speeds up, forward when it brakes, and sideways in turns. Your eyes then see the motion your inner ear feels.\n\nFor best results, sit facing forward, keep the device steady and start the cues before you begin to feel unwell.</string>

